# Sanaro's stage N11 (docs/sanaro.md section 20): the weaker-fire progression. pc-sanaro-n09 (results
# on claude/pc-sanaro-n09-results, 2026-11-02) was flat arm by arm: B480 +0.10 +-0.33 (survival 23.8
# to 28.2), K65 +0.06, B560 +0.02, K80 -0.08. Weaker fire buys 2-4 points of survival at no APS cost,
# and the BAND steps lean up (B560 +0.02, B480 +0.10). Leigh 2026-11-02: small increments work, think
# progression. So this card climbs that slope in small steps on twice the seeds, to read 0.1-0.2 APS.
#   ./queue.sh run pc-sanaro-n10        (or  .\queue.ps1 run pc-sanaro-n10)
# Run it from master:
#   git checkout master && git pull
# One bench queue, RoboRumble workers at 0, unpinned, 12 workers. Every step resumes; no step needs
# a decision. Nothing here touches Hadur, Saor, TwinSaor, Deise, JayLexi or Eveimear. No teach run.
# Arms (sanaro-arms/arms.txt, on 0.3's source, all 249 B: BAND is one constant, the table a string):
#   S3    Sanaro 0.3 as it ships (control)
#   B480  BAND 480 again, on fresh seeds (n09's best)
#   B400  BAND 400: 0.1 past 400, x1 to 200, x2 to 133
#   B320  BAND 320: 0.1 past 320, x1 to 160, x2 to 107
#   B4K8  BAND 480 and the table x 0.8
# Live-shaped census: 43 fields x 20 fresh seeds (base 28000) = 860 battles an arm, about 50 min an
# arm at n09's 1,050 an hour (95% on a difference about +-0.23). About 4 h 10 min in all.
# Read against S3. An arm passes when the low end of its difference is above zero (SANARO-13). The
# best passing arm is 0.4 on Leigh's word. If B480 repeats near +0.1 but misses the bar, the next
# step pools n09's and n10's B480 battles (1,290 against 1,290).
# Stop rules on every battle step (docs/bench/watch.md; halt, every battle fought is kept and a
# rerun resumes):
# - 20 failed battles (a broken jar).
# - No battle in 30 minutes (a hung step).
# - 40+ skipped turns a battle over the last 100 (the PR #331 build-up).
# A halt at worst leaves the rest of that step and the steps after it unrun: at most 4,300 battles,
# about 4 h 10 min. There is no early finish on score. A census step is one robot, so there is no
# arm to compare against before the read. ALERT opens an issue for Leigh on a stop.

set MVN = mvn -q -Drobocode.version=1.11.1 compile exec:java
set OUT = ../docs/bench/local
set ALERT = lgriffin
set ARMS = S3,B480,B400,B320,B4K8

prep | (cd .. && mvn -q -DskipTests install -pl sanaro -am) && mkdir -p work/sanaro-n10 && cp ../sanaro/target/hadur117.nano.Sanaro_0.3.jar opponents/ && ./fetch-opponents.sh --set nanomelee-field.txt && for f in melee-census-317/f*.txt; do ./fetch-opponents.sh --set "$f" || exit 1; done

arms | SANARO_RUN=n10 bash tools/sanaro_arms.sh live 20 28000 ${ARMS}
  after: prep

live-S3 | ${MVN} "-Dexec.args=@work/sanaro-n10/live-S3.args"
  after: arms
  watch: battles=860
  stop: fails 20
  stop: stall 30m
  stop: skips 40 over 100

live-B480 | ${MVN} "-Dexec.args=@work/sanaro-n10/live-B480.args"
  after: live-S3
  watch: battles=860
  stop: fails 20
  stop: stall 30m
  stop: skips 40 over 100

live-B400 | ${MVN} "-Dexec.args=@work/sanaro-n10/live-B400.args"
  after: live-B480
  watch: battles=860
  stop: fails 20
  stop: stall 30m
  stop: skips 40 over 100

live-B320 | ${MVN} "-Dexec.args=@work/sanaro-n10/live-B320.args"
  after: live-B400
  watch: battles=860
  stop: fails 20
  stop: stall 30m
  stop: skips 40 over 100

live-B4K8 | ${MVN} "-Dexec.args=@work/sanaro-n10/live-B4K8.args"
  after: live-B320
  watch: battles=860
  stop: fails 20
  stop: stall 30m
  stop: skips 40 over 100

read-live | python3 tools/sanaro_read.py --work-root work/sanaro-n10 --field live --arms ${ARMS} --control S3 --only work/sanaro-n10/live/micro.txt --live 66.44 > ${OUT}/sanaro-n10-live.md
  after: live-B4K8

pr | bash tools/open_results_pr.sh claude/pc-sanaro-n10-results "Sanaro stage N11: the weaker-fire progression against 0.3" ${OUT}/sanaro-n10-live.md ${OUT}/sanaro-n10-live-*.md
  after: read-live
